WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.730
Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament Arena

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.730
I won!

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.810
That's amazing!

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.110
Congratulations on the win, Nat-chan!

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.530
Congrats! That was fast.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.740
Thanks!

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.890
So Ei-chan is leading in the second set?

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.350
He just made his first break.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.490
He changed the tempo by mixing up his shots.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.510
It was a very Ei-chan-like play.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.460
So he's able to change the pace well, huh?

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.770
Game: Maruo. 4-1.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:35.930
Second set!

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.390
<i>Yes, I held!</i>

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.760
<i>But I've still broken only once.</i>

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.980
Araya 2-4 Maruo

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.480
Araya 2-5 Maruo

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.980
Araya 3-5 Maruo

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.500
<i>Set point!</i>

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.480
<i>If I win this, we'll be going to the final set!</i>

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.400
<i>I'll go for...</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.490
Another drop shot!

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.640
He's already over there!

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.490
That's so risky!

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.240
He got it!

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.890
Second set winner: Maruo.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.460
Score: 6-3.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.320
Yes!

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:12.850
<i>My moves are getting better 
every time I return his drop shots.</i>

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.960
<i>Maybe it's because it reminds 
me of facing Takuma.</i>

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.580
<i>Even though it's the prefectural final,</i>

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.810
<i>I honestly didn't think my engine would 
start since I'm not facing Takuma.</i>

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:28.910
<i>I could never admit that to 
my teammates who left...</i>

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.510
<i>But I honestly couldn't do it.</i>

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.660
<i>But this match reminded me</i>

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.240
<i>how I felt when I first started playing tennis.</i>

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.890
<i>Playing you, not Takuma, in this final round</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.610
<i>made me remember that.</i>

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.910
<i>In the end, I'm not doing this for someone,</i>

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.610
<i>or for honor, or anything like that.</i>

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.500
<i>I just hate to lose!</i>

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.510
Full Force Toward Adversity

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.680
Araya
Maruo

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.600
If you take this set, you win it all, Araya-san!

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.700
15-love.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.200
Yes!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.370
Araya's been getting more aces.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.620
That proves he's getting into the swing now.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.970
<i>This next one's a wide slice!</i>

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.750
<i>If I get it, hit it flat and deep!</i>

00:03:58.960 --> 00:03:59.760
<i>I did it!</i>

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.060
<i>Once I have the advantage,</i>

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>I'll hit a shallow slice crosscourt!</i>

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.790
<i>If he moves up, then...</i>

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.930
<i>Lob it!</i>

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:07.810
<i>How's that?!</i>

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:12.790
30-love.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.560
Yes!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.300
He lost his balance, 
but made it in time to counter!

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.030
It's incredible! Araya's going full throttle!

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:22.790
<i>It's bad enough that his power 
and speed are on another level.</i>

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.080
<i>Now even his reaction time is getting faster!</i>

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.330
<i>Araya-kun is on his game, 
which is dangerous for me.</i>

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.320
<i>Right now, I have to calm down, 
think, and give myself more options.</i>

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.430
<i>To learn to trust my instincts more,</i>

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.580
<i>I'll trust my reason for now.</i>

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.350
Ei-chan looks like he's having fun, huh?

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.930
You may be right, Nat-chan.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.470
He has a habit of trying too 
hard sometimes, you know?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.430
Even during middle school 
ball sports meets and stuff.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.190
Okay, we've decided all of our positions.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.360
I think that'll do it.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.110
Yeah, so starting today, let's 
practice after school together!

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.260
Huh?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.250
Sorry, but I'll pass!

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.210
I've got my club.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.740
I'm busy, too.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.180
Oh, then whoever can stay...

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.920
It's just a ball sports meet.
It's not worth all that effort.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.230
You take everything too seriously.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.000
That's what's great about Ei-chan, though.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.750
Let's have a little more fun with it.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.670
It's soccer, so if we don't do 
it as a team, there's no point!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.080
Right, Kageyama?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.220
I guess it's like...

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.510
He's on a different wavelength 
than other people.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:34.430
Which is exactly why I think 
he's truly having fun right now.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.400
There's someone answering Ei-chan's
best efforts with his own best efforts.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.340
And as he gets stronger, 
he'll find more of those.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.980
Through tennis, he's discovered the fun of

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.700
really going all-out against someone.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.950
Araya
Maruo

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.940
<i>After playing against you 
for this long, I can tell...</i>

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.210
<i>You want to go pro, don't you?</i>

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.460
<i>All the more reason I can't let you win.</i>

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.490
<i>No matter when you change your pace,</i>

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.250
<i>no matter where you control your shots...</i>

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.460
<i>In the end, my speed will catch up to you!</i>

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.750
40-30.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:09.470
Yes!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.940
<i>I have to find more ways to attack...</i>

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.280
<i>But don't panic.</i>

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.790
<i>Just concentrate and...</i>

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.360
Game: Maruo. 4-all.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.470
That's amazing. Neither 
of them is backing down.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.080
It'll come down to whoever wins 
two games in a row first.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.950
Araya-san! You've gotta hold serve now!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.080
Bring it home, unseeded kid!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.590
Araya
Maruo

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.590
There's no tie-breaker, 
even though it's 6-all?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.860
In this tournament, for the final set,

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.710
they play until there's a two-game defecit.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:51.750
So does that mean if they 
both continue to hold,

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.050
they can go up to 6-all, 7-all, and so forth?

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:55.850
Yes.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.310
So it ends up being a test of endurance?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.600
Doesn't that put Ei-chan 
at a clear disadvantage?

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:07.710
Out!

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.470
Game: Araya. 5-4.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.320
Final set.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.570
Yeah!

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.870
All right, Araya-san! Take the
next game and finish this!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.280
It's still a tie!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.120
Make sure you hold, Maruo!

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.420
<i>Oh... It's time to change ends.</i>

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.290
<i>Why am I zoning out?!</i>

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.750
<i>If he breaks next, I'm going to lose.</i>

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.090
<i>I'm getting enough sugar from the 
sports drinks, so it's not that.</i>

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:36.930
<i>I need to focus my energy and think harder!</i>

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.310
<i>No, calm down.</i>

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.190
<i>There's another issue I need to deal with...</i>

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:43.980
<i>Exhaustion.</i>

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.680
<i>It's been over two hours 
since the match started.</i>

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.000
<i>Since I have to come up with new 
attack options after all his shots,</i>

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.420
<i>I'm using my brain far more than usual.</i>

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:56.330
<i>So my mind's getting tired before my body.</i>

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.490
Take Down Araya File
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power 
on his side, it's normal to lose from time to time.
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:06.040
<i>But if I don't break in the final 
set, we'll go into overtime.</i>

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.040
Araya
Maruo

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.700
<i>I wish I could play without 
relying on my brain now...</i>

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:13.110
<i>But I'm still trying to find attack 
options through trial and error.</i>

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.940
<i>I can't just play without thinking.</i>

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:20.370
<i>Still, I made it this far against Araya-kun...</i>

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.490
<i>I don't want to concede and 
lose because I got tired.</i>

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:26.370
<i>I'd rather die!</i>

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:36.570
Time!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:45.910
<i>At any rate, my opponent is Araya-kun, 
whose weapon is his physical stamina.</i>

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.380
<i>I'll be at a disadvantage in overtime.</i>

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.840
<i>I have no choice but to use the 
shortest, fastest method.</i>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.230
He's running up after serving!

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.050
<i>I need to break up Araya-kun's tempo</i>

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.600
<i>and use shots that'll win 
points as quickly as possible!</i>

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.100
<i>He lobbed on a return?!</i>

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.950
<i>As if I'd miss that!</i>

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:07.100
<i>If you're close to your limit, 
I don't need to rush the match!</i>

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.340
<i>It's deep...</i>

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.860
<i>But if I want a quick, decisive win, 
it's gotta be in this shot!</i>

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.150
Yes!

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:17.950
Wow, he controlled it even 
though it was that deep!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.410
But if that lob were about 30 centimeters 
deeper, it would've been over.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.880
<i>I can't believe Araya-kun would 
return immediately with a lob.</i>

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.660
<i>Did he figure out that I want to 
win points as quickly as possible?</i>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.490
Fault!

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:33.420
So close!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:37.780
<i>An ace would be the best 
way to score quickly.</i>

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.210
<i>But it's not something you 
can just pull off so easily.</i>

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.910
<i>I'll go deep and accurate 
for my second serve.</i>

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.610
<i>It's now a ground stroke battle!</i>

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:55.080
<i>During my serve game, 
I'll take my time, as always,</i>

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.110
<i>and keep looking for new attack options.</i>

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.560
30-love.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.590
Yes!

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:08.370
<i>I'll use as much time as I can 
between points to rest my mind.</i>

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.090
<i>After all this, he's playing defensively now.</i>

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:19.430
<i>He must realize I'm trying to 
win points as soon as possible.</i>

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.660
30-15.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.580
30-all.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.270
<i>And when he sees an opportunity, 
he goes right for it!</i>

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.050
<i>But that makes it easier for me.</i>

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.270
40-30.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.770
<i>I'll direct all my energy 
into going in for the attack!</i>

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.340
Game: Maruo. 5-all.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.420
Final set.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:40.560
Yes! He got it!

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.910
Ei-chan, nice hold!

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.430
<i>I finally got it.</i>

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.390
<i>Next, I have to break, no matter what.</i>

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.080
Araya
Maruo

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.080
<i>If I break here, it'll be 6-5.</i>

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:53.300
<i>Then if I hold the next game, it'll be 7-5.</i>

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.420
<i>Regardless, I have to finish this 
while I still have the chance!</i>

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.090
<i>I won't change my style again.</i>

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.890
<i>I'll raise the stakes and 
be as risky as I can.</i>

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.150
<i>Prepare myself...</i>

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:06.880
<i>Center!</i>

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:09.890
<i>I got it!</i>

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.730
Love-15.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:13.900
Yes!

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:15.510
That's amazing!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.660
He saw the ball's course and went for it!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.440
That's pretty bold for Maruo.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.590
Was he going for the winner?

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:25.080
To be accurate, he probably 
<i>has</i> to go for it at this point.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.850
<i>Going for an ace right 
from his first serve...</i>

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.080
<i>There's no mistaking it.</i>

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.950
<i>You're trying to rush the match.</i>

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.990
<i>There are infinite options for changing the pace.</i>

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:42.090
<i>I was honestly getting irritated at 
your nondescript style of tennis.</i>

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.100
<i>But adding to that
a need to rush the match</i>

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.990
<i>severely decreases your options!</i>

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.180
15-all.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:56.610
30-15.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.110
40-15.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.610
40-30.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.370
Game: Araya. 6-5.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.620
Araya
Maruo

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.620
Final set.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.780
<i>Damn... I failed to break.</i>

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:10.870
<i>He sees right through me.</i>

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.660
<i>If you're coming after me 
by rushing the pace,</i>

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.880
<i>it's obvious that I'll fight back defensively.</i>

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.880
6-all.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.870
7-6.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:24.890
7-all.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.220
Game: Araya. 8-7.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.890
Araya
Maruo

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:28.890
Final set.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.080
This has turned into an intense match.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.890
How long is this going to go on for?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:34.290
Ei-chan...

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.640
<i>Crap... If I concentrate on one point 
for too long, my eyes get blurry.</i>

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:50.910
<i>But I can't do anything if Araya-kun 
keeps playing defensively like this.</i>

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.980
<i>Is it worth taking even 
bigger risks right now?</i>

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:55.420
Time!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.420
<i>Oh... It's already time.</i>

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:02.930
<i>Fault!</i>

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.950
Double fault!

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.080
Love-15.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.890
<i>The risk was too high!</i>

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.890
<i>It's not like you to miss 
at a time like this, Bro.</i>

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:22.810
<i>You feel pressured because you have to 
continue hitting quickly and powerfully.</i>

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.870
<i>In other words, the difference 
between our physiques</i>

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:28.540
<i>is the difference between our ability!</i>

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.650
Love-30.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.170
<i>Love-30...</i>

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.730
<i>If he takes this next one, it'll be love-40.</i>

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.420
<i>He'll have triple match point.</i>

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.190
<i>Damn... What do I do?</i>

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.860
<i>In the moment I have to think the most,</i>

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:54.440
<i>my brain won't focus.</i>

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.980
<i>He'll lower his risk here.</i>

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.740
15-30.

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.360
Huh?

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.980
Wasn't that really fast just now?

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:12.620
Yeah.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.820
<i>I see...</i>

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.700
<i>I can hit serves without thinking.</i>

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:31.140
30-all.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:35.100
Again! This time he hit a winner 
after an amazing serve!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.890
He just won two points in 
a row just from his serve!

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.230
It's a big deal that he caught up 
without getting to match point.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.460
Maruo still has that much strength left?

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.820
No way. That can't be.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:48.790
<i>It's working.</i>

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.820
<i>I was suddenly able to hit the way I wanted.</i>

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:58.830
<i>Is that because I was forced into using 
my instincts after my mind became tired?</i>

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.230
He ran up after serving!

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.600
40-30.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.080
Hey, it happened again.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.740
Has Maruo actually recovered?

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.720
If he keeps going like this, 
he can totally break next!

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:18.680
<i>No, it's most likely that he's 
too fatigued to use his reason,</i>

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.310
<i>so he has no choice left 
but to trust his instincts.</i>

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:27.730
Instinct

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.110
<i>The extreme fatigue plus his anxiety</i>

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.730
<i>is miraculously balancing the scales 
between his reason and instincts.</i>

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:32.240
<i>If that's so, this situation 
won't last very long.</i>

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.020
<i>He changed his method 
from breaking up the tempo</i>

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:37.580
<i>to taking riskier, simpler shots.</i>

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:42.430
<i>I've seen countless players get a second 
wind once they resolved to lose.</i>

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:46.490
<i>That last bit of resistance isn't 
something to take lightly.</i>

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.130
<i>This is it.</i>

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.920
<i>This is when we decide who wins!</i>

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:57.640
<i>It's shallow!</i>

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:02.270
Out!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.160
Yeah!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:03.680
Deuce!

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:06.560
Whoa! Now Araya got him back!

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:07.780
<i>Damn...</i>

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:10.520
<i>I can't return that crosscourt 
forehand on instinct alone.</i>

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.760
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:16.010
<i>Given how tired I am, my only option
is to force him into hitting backhands.</i>

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:22.830
He forced his way into the shot!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:28.080
<i>Crap! Hit the left-handed forehand 
a beat faster than normal and...</i>

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:31.840
<i>Stop!</i>

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:37.690
Advantage: Araya!

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:38.600
Yeah!

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.600
This is it! Match point!

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.460
<i>What was that?</i>

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:44.730
<i>My body suddenly felt really heavy.</i>

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:48.090
<i>His instincts stopped him, huh?</i>

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:51.900
<i>They prioritized resting his body 
over continuing to battle.</i>

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.530
<i>Just because it got heavy 
doesn't mean my body won't move.</i>

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.410
<i>I can still do this.</i>

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.160
End it here, Araya!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.910
Hang in there, Ei-chan!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.850
<i>Fault?!</i>

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:37.360
<i>He ran around it!</i>

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.200
<i>The left forehand is going to my backhand!</i>

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.490
Game, set, and match.

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:12.770
Winner: Araya. Score: 6-3, 3-6, 9-7.

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:16.280
Yes!

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.280
<i>Huh? Is it over already?</i>

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.480
Hey, Maruo!

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:27.490
Are you okay?

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.110
Yeah... S-Sorry.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:45.210
Seems like you're no longer a no-name player.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:46.690
Take a look around you.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.590
That was so moving!

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:53.530
That was an incredible match!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:54.920
You're the best, Araya!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.490
No, Maruo's the hero today!

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.200
You both better go national!

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.200
Ei-chan, you did great!

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.940
Araya, you finally did it!

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:07.950
Araya-san, congratulations!

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.850
<i>Yeah... It's really over.</i>

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:17.840
Well done!

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.840
Okay...

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.560
I think you did the right 
thing by changing up the pace

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.430
to deal with a strong arm like that.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:29.420
It's normally not something 
that can be learned so quickly.

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.850
You were great.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.870
In terms of Kanto, a loss hurts,

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.570
but establishing a clear goal 
is a real achievement.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.020
Right...

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.110
Listen, Maruo-kun.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:48.580
I watched you and Araya-kun 
face each other six months ago.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:54.340
It's astounding how much you closed 
the vast gap between you two.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.460
You didn't win,

00:19:56.790 --> 00:20:01.470
but there's no doubt that you've 
improved the most in all of Kanagawa.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.700
That's right!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.550
You were able to get a nationally ranked
player on the ropes! That's amazing!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.480
That means you can compete 
on a national level, Ei-chan.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.030
Do you have a second?

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.480
What... Huh?

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.340
Iwasa-kun?

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:23.540
It's the prefectural finals, and I thought 
it might be nice to sketch outside.

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:27.370
I was planning on going home after taking some reference photos,

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:31.250
but after watching you, I wanted to 
revise what I said to you in the past.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.040
Six months ago, after our match,

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:37.880
I said to you

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:41.210
that just having fun wouldn't 
be enough to beat Araya.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:46.090
But I was wrong.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:50.730
I realized myself, after I 
decided to pursue my own art,

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.750
that if you're going to dedicate 
your life to something,

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:58.610
nothing propels you more than the 
sensation of having fun while doing it.

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.580
Every single time you hit a wall,

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:05.860
you gave it your all to 
find ways to overcome it.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.120
The way you continued to get 
back up looked as though

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.120
you were enjoying the match 
more than anyone else.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:20.880
Perhaps the reason you were able 
to put up such a fight against Araya

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.460
is because you were enjoying 
tennis more than anyone.

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.430
Thank you.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:37.210
But I still lost.

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:38.940
No matter how much I enjoyed it...

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:41.070
Or how much stronger I got...

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.940
That's not good enough.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:44.920
Unless I can win...

00:22:03.310 --> 00:22:07.020
<i>We will now commence the Kanagawa Junior 
Tennis Tournament awards ceremony.</i>

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:11.270
<i>All winners, please meet at Court 1.</i>

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:16.240
All right, stop crying! It's 
time for the awards ceremony!

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.040
You should be proud of yourself today.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:20.040
R-Right.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:27.070
<i>Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament 
winner: Araya Hiroshi.</i>

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:31.950
Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament Results
U-18 Girls                             U-18 Boys
Winner: Takasaki Natsu     Winner: Araya Hiroshi
Runner-up: Sakurai Rei      Runner-up: Maruo Eiichiro
Top 4: Kosaka Akiko (STC)     Top 4: Mogami Norihiko (Shonan Technical Academy)
Hasegawa Mako (Miyagawa T.A.)      Inoue Kiichi (Minamikawa TC)

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:29.730
<i>Runner-up: Maruo Eiichiro.</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:02.120
We're going to start practical training today?

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:02.610
Hey.

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:04.330
What? Iwasa-kun?

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:06.080
Miyagawa-kun and Mogami-kun, too?

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:07.220
And even Araya-kun!

00:24:07.220 --> 00:24:08.460
What? Why?

00:24:08.460 --> 00:24:10.970
It looks like we're going to 
train together more often.

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:15.090
I'm here because they agreed to allow 
me to sketch during my downtime.

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.240
This is amazing.

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:18.480
If we do this frequently,

00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:20.410
it means we can play a lot of matches!

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:22.740
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Gathering of Rivals

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.240
"Gathering of Rivals."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:30.500
End
